    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8757" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cŏagmentātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		coagmento, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a joining</i> or <i>connecting
				together; a connection</i>, <i>combination</i>,
				<i>union</i> (several times in Cic.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">elsewh. rare): corporis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Univ. 5 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non dissolubilis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					N. D. 1, 8, 20</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">naturae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 46, 119</span></i>
			.—<i>Plur.</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 2, 9,
				11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 36, 22, 51, §
		172</span></i>.</div>
